		summary = "**Northern Cyprus**, officially the **Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus** (**TRNC**), is a [[De facto and de jure|de facto]] state comprising the northern third of the island of Cyprus. It is recognised only by [[Turkey]], with the international community considering it territory of the [[Cyprus|Republic of Cyprus]] under Turkish military occupation. It extends from Cape Apostolos Andreas (the tip of the Karpass Peninsula) in the northeast to Morphou Bay in the northwest, with Cape Kormakitis at its westernmost point and the Kokkina exclave west of the mainland. A buffer zone controlled by the [[United Nations|UN]] forms a barrier between both sides of the island and runs through Nicosia, the island's largest city and the capital of both sides.",
